# CODEOWNERS — bifrost (21StarkCom/bifrost)
# A CODEOWNERS match assigns the listed owners as reviewers. Order matters: the
# LAST matching pattern wins for a given path.
#
# NOT AN ENFORCED MERGE GATE TODAY. `require_code_owner_reviews` is false and
# `required_approving_review_count` is 0 on `main` (measured 2026-09-20; see
# docs/SECURITY.md §3 and §5 for why, on a one-operator repo). These lines record
# OWNERSHIP — who must look at a path — and become a gate the day a second
# maintainer exists and §5's APPLY block is run. What actually holds the
# high-trust paths meanwhile is the mandatory `/code-review xhigh --fix` round.
#
# Trust model: every artifact BODY is instruction text injected into a developer's
# agent, and every mcp/ entry is a command spawned on a developer's machine. Those
# are the highest-trust surfaces (spec §7.4, §14). The policy for them is TWO
# distinct approvals — a CODEOWNERS entry alone only forces "review from a Code
# Owner" and still merges on one approval, so it needs repo-wide
# `required_approving_review_count = 2` alongside it. bifrost has one human, so
# every rule below resolves to @aryeh-stark and the count stays 0.

# ── Default: the maintainer reviews anything not matched below ──
*                               @aryeh-stark

# ── High-trust artifact BODIES (skills/commands/agents) ──
# Policy: maintainer + a second reviewer.
catalog/**/skills/**            @aryeh-stark
catalog/**/commands/**          @aryeh-stark
catalog/**/agents/**            @aryeh-stark

# ── MCP = code execution on the developer's machine — highest trust ──
**/mcp/**                       @aryeh-stark

# ── Engine + generated output + schema + provenance ──
engine/**                       @aryeh-stark
schema/**                       @aryeh-stark

# ── MCP command-allowlist source — additions reviewed by the maintainer (§15.4) ──
# Listed AFTER engine/** so it wins (last match) and is unmistakably called out:
# every entry added here widens the set of binaries an MCP server may spawn.
engine/internal/validate/allowlist.go     @aryeh-stark
engine/internal/validate/toolsallow.go    @aryeh-stark
dist/claude/**                  @aryeh-stark
index.json                      @aryeh-stark
bundles/**                      @aryeh-stark

# ── Security/CI governance ──
.github/workflows/**            @aryeh-stark
CODEOWNERS                      @aryeh-stark
docs/SECURITY.md                @aryeh-stark
.gitleaks.toml                  @aryeh-stark
